questions.explain:
A range-based for loop hands you each value but never says which subscript it came from. To copy `a[i]` into `b[i]` you need i, to say where in b the value goes. So this task needs a counting loop:
```
for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)
    b[i] = a[i];
```
Adding up and displaying need only the values. Doubling in place also works without subscripts, using a reference range variable: `for (int &x : a) x *= 2;`.

